is is more an addendum to the main text. 60 pages is probably the shortest product we've seen for Mummy in either edition so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/144748/Lore-of-the-Deceived\" target=\"_blank\">Lore of the Deceived</a> is shorter, sitting at 13 pages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T14:55:02-07:00","id":1492185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492180#post1492180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/144748/Lore-of-the-Deceived&amp;quot;]Lore</a> of the Deceived[/URL] is shorter, sitting at 13 pages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything to add concerning the new supplement? Just curious","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T15:27:32-07:00","id":1492188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492108#post1492108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dunno how I feel about it, honestly. Seems decent as far the writing so far, but my oh my is it brief. Like, I was expecting something akin to an ST guide or something but this is more an addendum to the main text. 60 pages is probably the shortest product we've seen for Mummy in either edition so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you there. I enjoyed what we had, but I would\u2019ve also enjoyed one or two examples of Seba, Neoliths, and Ankhs in order to have a better idea on how to make them distinct from other relics. Sure we have the Deceived content to help with Seba, but it still would\u2019ve been nice to see some vessels in the pdf all the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T17:57:04-07:00","id":1492192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492185#post1492185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anything to add concerning the new supplement? Just curious</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, yeah, Butcher Demon Transfiguration is the best kind of anime bullshit.<br /> <br /> More coming later, I want to hype this book up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T18:56:08-07:00","id":1492194,"title":"","content":"Tread The Crimson Field Eternal is delightfully Doom Slayer-ish too, it has the potential to be very busted.. depending on how that Sekhem burn thing works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T21:11:57-07:00","id":1492338,"title":"","content":"So we can get some hype up, let's give a run down of what is in the book and what's my take on it.<br /> <br /> As a broad explanation, the Book of Lasting Death is mostly a wide variety of alternative characters, including enemies but more often in the 'frain of deliciously swiss army knife for casting, all of them handily filling in as foil, adversary, and ally (Yes, even the Deceived) as well as being imminently playable. There's definitely some welcome world building, and definitely some new toys for people to play with, but I would still by and large look at it from that inital point of view, and I would still hew it being a hair bit more for Storytellers than Players-not that players can't or won't get anything out of (again, pretty much everything here is playable), but it's definitely more useful in the toolbox.<br /> <br /> Chapter 1 is dedicated to the Minor Guilds, and I will go over them in brief.<br /> <br /> The inclusion of the Akhem-Urtu, aka the Decieved, into the category of the Minor Guilds has always been something that causes me to squint in consternation, but while the argument can still be made that doing so downplays one of the best organized dark-mirror antagonists of Chronicles, most other concerns can be put to rest regarding their entry here. Sure, it doesn't have the space to serve diehard fans the way they might want, but it very neatly and summarily reintroduces the Restless Stars in a very satisfying way that communicates their Big Deal-ness as much as humanly possible in the circumstances. If that sounds like a backhanded knock, it's not, it's a legitimately really good reintroduction of the middle class liberal arts major boogeymen, and in some ways it's actually an improvement, particularly when it comes to mechanics. Showiness is not a virtue for an antagonist defined by subversion of cosmic desire, exploitation of memory, and in general being the boogeyman, but if there was something lacking from the Decieved, it was the power of iconics in their reveal, and BoLD delivers very well on that front. The new Utterance, Color From Void, may hew a little toward's the Painter's verbiage, enough so that people who know what I'm talking about probably wonder how it works for any of the other six Temakhs, but it's otherwise a very good power to evoke the Deceived, and the Nameless Things of the third tier in particular is just utterly delicious as a minion type antagonist. Wielder of Names is positively elegant for how simply and directly it addresses the Ren-Hekau and how it's used to make a big deal out of the Deceived, and I don't say that as a slam towards previous attempts, it's just honestly the best delivered take on the subject. Even the affinity As Whispers In The Night, this edition's Face of Endless Lies, feels much more brand appropriate, since the edtion's overall move from the &quot;mind is the body is the mind so all Mental Flaws are accompanied by Physical Flaws&quot; means that this one can make it more like an affectation of the name, of the way one <i>gets</i> the information about a person, rather than simply be a doppelganger power, and that it twists Fate to protect the Embodiment of Vision so casually goes a long way to make them feel powerful in that low-key, behind the scenes way.<br /> <br /> I also had some hesitation about Military Guild Kher-Minu, because the way Mummy handled the subject of the Nameless Empire's military appealed to me on a lot of layers and in a lot of different ways, and making them some kind of Guild, let alone Arisen, threatened that, but worry not--the second-string engine of the empire not only retains the form of address that made them interesting (and true) previously in their capacity, but also make for an interesting and fickle character type, whose bloodlust and only-in-some-ways well-earned bitterness towards the Major Guilds contrasted with a thorough understanding of their role and the reasoning makes them a really vivacious character type to read and implement in a number of ways. Their powerset is also just very deeply satisfying, with Dust Beneath Feet and Guardian Wrath being innate just being solid decision making, Butcher Demon Transfiguration is, as mentioned, the best kind of anime bullshit, and in an instance where I'm glad systems glitched so I could read Korogra, Tread the Crimson Field Eternal is also the best Doom/boomer-shooter-esque bullshit as well. Honestly enjoyed the military way more than I expected to. Certainly the justification to have chararcter who takes &quot;Mercy is a mistake/ Peace was never an option&quot; as actual response as interesting character, whether fucking hey-shit-you've-got-a-point or (as I take more often) fucking shit-why-are-you-like-this.<br /> <br /> We'll pick up tomorrow, shall we?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-05-2022, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T12:25:21-07:00","id":1492381,"title":"","content":"Thanks Arcane!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T12:05:22-07:00","id":1492706,"title":"","content":"I had a few questions regarding the differences between 1e and 2e Decieved that Im hoping someone has the answers to.<br /> <br /> So, we know that a LOT of the lore behind the Devieved remains unchanged, as do the Temakh. In 1e, each Decieved looked weird and alien as a default, and had to rely on powers to appear as anything but obvious. That seemed counterintuitive as heck in 1e. From what Arc was saying earlier, does this mean that in 2e that has been scrapped? Are Decieved no more or less weird looking than most mummies? Do their sybaris forms look more like the 1e alienness rather than have it be physical?<br /> <br /> Likewise mentioned by Arc, my two PC Decieved are a Musician and a Philosopher. Would they still use a visual medium for the Decieved Utterance? Or could a recording of music or a spoken arguement work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","user":"Cleverest of Things","date":". 09-09-2022, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T17:29:42-07:00","id":1492727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492706#post1492706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, we know that a LOT of the lore behind the Devieved remains unchanged, as do the Temakh. In 1e, each Decieved looked weird and alien as a default, and had to rely on powers to appear as anything but obvious. That seemed counterintuitive as heck in 1e. From what Arc was saying earlier, does this mean that in 2e that has been scrapped? Are Decieved no more or less weird looking than most mummies? Do their sybaris forms look more like the 1e alienness rather than have it be physical?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per 2e core, the temakh is &quot;an alien and corrupted beast of fluid form,&quot; and the mechanical change in how Sybaris works in general has translated the Deceived's specific twist on it into imposing a two-dice penalty on rolls to resist Sybaris in their presence as people sense the strangeness about them; the Maar-Kherit have picked up the slack on particularly overt supernatural trouble, being mechanically incapable of inflicting Sybaris less intense than Terror Sybaris.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Likewise mentioned by Arc, my two PC Decieved are a Musician and a Philosopher. Would they still use a visual medium for the Decieved Utterance? Or could a recording of music or a spoken arguement work? </div> </div> </div>The first Tier of Color from Void, at least, affects a Crafts <i>or Expression</i> roll to create a work of art, and the way it works is such that you can probably substitute the appropriate sense for &quot;see&quot; in the Tier's description. The other two Tiers are more specifically visually-oriented, but the Deceived's 2e mechanics are less particular and granular about the artforms they deal with; their single-point Pillar recovery method just involves inspiring another character to create something, and the sidebar on Temakh Concepts mostly suggests using the temakh's artform to inform goals and the types of people they surround themselves with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T21:06:45-07:00","id":1492856,"title":"","content":"Maar-Kherit are probably my favorite addition to the game. While we don't have rules for there relics ankhs they seem pretty simple to understand which is healing, restoration, rejuvenation.<br /> <br /> Though I do have to ask people here if the Maar-Kherit and Deceived are also considered timeless or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T21:33:13-07:00","id":1492857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492856#post1492856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maar-Kherit are probably my favorite addition to the game. While we don't have rules for there relics ankhs they seem pretty simple to understand which is healing, restoration, rejuvenation.<br /> <br /> Though I do have to ask people here if the Maar-Kherit and Deceived are also considered timeless or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maar-kherit are endless, not sure about the deceived. However it's possible they are as every other minor guild is endless too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T21:43:28-07:00","id":1492859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492857#post1492857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maar-kherit are endless, not sure about the deceived. However it's possible they are as every other minor guild is endless too</div> </div> </div> </div>The Deceived are <i>eternal</i>.<br /> <br /> Not that this book has the space to discuss the distinction.<br /> <br /> but yeah, the Maar-Kerit and Akhem-Urtu are also Timeless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T21:48:50-07:00","id":1492860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492859#post1492859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Deceived are <i>eternal</i>.<br /> <br /> Not that this book has the space to discuss the distinction.<br /> <br /> but yeah, the Maar-Kerit and Akhem-Urtu are also Timeless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crap my bad. But 1st edition lacked timelessness, so while eternal, are they still part of the endless chronologically speaking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T21:55:17-07:00","id":1492862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492860#post1492860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Crap my bad. But 1st edition lacked timelessness, so while eternal, are they still part of the endless chronologically speaking?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492859#post1492859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but yeah, the Maar-Kerit and Akhem-Urtu are also Timeless.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T21:57:52-07:00","id":1492863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492859#post1492859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Deceived are <i>eternal</i>.<br /> <br /> Not that this book has the space to discuss the distinction.<br /> <br /> but yeah, the Maar-Kerit and Akhem-Urtu are also Timeless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the info wanted to make sure seeing as it mentions the wadja are not timeless and wasn't sure the two others and to an extent the Kherit minu were also timeless.<br /> <br /> Though I do have a couple more questions though which is how do the Maar-Kherit gain Sekhem seeing as it mentions they can't eat relics?<br /> <br /> Furthermore its mentioned that the Maar-Kherit have a high contagion of diseases, I am assuming this isn't mechanized and more of a storytelling thing to ensure that a Maar-Kherit can hang with a Arisen group as well as cult?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T22:08:30-07:00","id":1492865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492863#post1492863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the info wanted to make sure seeing as it mentions the wadja are not timeless and wasn't sure the two others and to an extent the Kherit minu were also timeless.<br /> <br /> Though I do have a couple more questions though which is how do the Maar-Kherit gain Sekhem seeing as it mentions they can't eat relics?<br /> <br /> Furthermore its mentioned that the Maar-Kherit have a high contagion of diseases, I am assuming this isn't mechanized and more of a storytelling thing to ensure that a Maar-Kherit can hang with a Arisen group as well as cult?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Maar-Kerit gain Sekhem by-wait, they just don't.<br /> <br /> And the disease is Very Much Mechanized. There are mechanics for how they can have a cult (basically if you survive the main way of catching the plague, you gain immunity), and of course the Arisen fake sneeze at disease, but playing the Maar-Kherit* is a very Promethean-like experience.<br /> <br /> *Wasting away again in Maar-Kherit-a-ville.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T15:05:14-07:00","id":1492928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492859#post1492859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Deceived are <i>eternal</i>.<br /> <br /> Not that this book has the space to discuss the distinction.<br /> <br /> but yeah, the Maar-Kerit and Akhem-Urtu are also Timeless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since a LOT of what made the Decieved distinctly even more eternal than the Arisen now apply to all mummies, and Timelessness was added on top to boot, I had assumed that now all Arisen are on the same footing. So, you mean the Decieved are still distinctly even more unkillable than the Arisen? Does that mean more like.. literally nothing can stop the Decieved from resurrection, even lack of body, cultists, etc? Or does it mean even MORE? So.. like maybe.. perceiving ALL lifetimes bit by bit as memory increases rather than one? Perhaps the Decieved always awakens the moment a Temakh reaches the fivefold Decieved and drags it into the mortal plane? Perhaps when having Low Memory, a Decieved doesnt precisely forget who they are so much as forget they are not the eternal temakh?<br /> <br /> Please, PLEASE tell me someone has pitched a Night Horrors style Mummy book, with more details about the Decieved, Shuanksen, Amkhata (colossi!!), Judge Avatars, Lifeless, Immortals, Fiends, and anomalies!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T15:14:47-07:00","id":1492929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492928#post1492928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since a LOT of what made the Decieved distinctly even more eternal than the Arisen now apply to all mummies, and Timelessness was added on top to boot, I had assumed that now all Arisen are on the same footing. So, you mean the Decieved are still distinctly even more unkillable than the Arisen? Does that mean more like.. literally nothing can stop the Decieved from resurrection, even lack of body, cultists, etc? Or does it mean even MORE? So.. like maybe.. perceiving ALL lifetimes bit by bit as memory increases rather than one? Perhaps the Decieved always awakens the moment a Temakh reaches the fivefold Decieved and drags it into the mortal plane? Perhaps when having Low Memory, a Decieved doesnt precisely forget who they are so much as forget they are not the eternal temakh?<br /> <br /> Please, PLEASE tell me someone has pitched a Night Horrors style Mummy book, with more details about the Decieved, Shuanksen, Amkhata (colossi!!), Judge Avatars, Lifeless, Immortals, Fiends, and anomalies!</div> </div> </div> </div>See &quot;Not that this book has space to discuss the distinction&quot; and apply Book of the Deceived's explanation in it's stead. It's mostly there to get in all that* Deceived feel in as small a space as possible. It does a good job, but that doesn't leave it space to go crazy.<br /> <br /> *urban gangsta flavour","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-12-2022, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T15:47:34-07:00","id":1492930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492862#post1492862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Where are they timeless though? I thought that only happened from the Rite of return?<br /> <br /> I mean timeless and endless in terms of one is not bound by linear time and one is. While only the wadjet are explicitly called out as not timeless, none of the other writeups lean toward it either","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T15:59:26-07:00","id":1492932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492930#post1492930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where are they timeless though? I thought that only happened from the Rite of return?<br /> <br /> I mean timeless and endless in terms of one is not bound by linear time and one is. While only the wadjet are explicitly called out as not timeless, none of the other writeups lean toward it either</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats a very good question, I second that. At first glance I assumed that the Decieved were Timeless.. but.. their existences arent a singular blip when theyre yanked out of timespace-free Duat storage the way the Arisen's are. Instead of being in an easily handbwaveable Elsewhere, Decieved spend their death cycles running around in Twilight where, theoretically, mummies, ghosts, sorcerers, mages, fiends, and the odd immortal and far roaming vampire or beast could find her. Seems to lean towards linearity.<br /> <br /> So, basically, instead of thinking of the Book of Lasting Death as replacing the 1e canon, instead view it as a small hotfix on the immediately noticeable changes (like the alien appearance and inborn Utterance) while the actual bulk of 1e is the more or less canon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T16:43:27-07:00","id":1492935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492930#post1492930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where are they timeless though? I thought that only happened from the Rite of return?<br /> <br /> I mean timeless and endless in terms of one is not bound by linear time and one is. While only the wadjet are explicitly called out as not timeless, none of the other writeups lean toward it either</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Akhem-Urtu were part of the Rite of Return. The Su-Menent screwed with their slice of it because they found out about the plan for the Shan'iatu Guildmasters to try and claim Judge Status over Life AND Death, but the explicit consequence of that is that the Shan'iatu were stuffed in with their servants.<br /> <br /> Endlessness is effectively the term for immortality not derived from the arts of Irem to those ends. Timelessness is explicitly the anti-relationship to time, and while it's usually a result of connection to Duat, disassociated from time as a rule, other forces can apply as well, such as the Deceived's relationship to Fate.<br /> <br /> And yeah, as BoLD goes, it's a hotfix. It updates everything that it updates, but doesn't assume everything else is left off the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T17:25:02-07:00","id":1492938,"title":"","content":"I do have to say I do quite like the strange, Terminator-ish direction they took the Visitors. That some of them actively want to help mankind while others want to dominate/destroy it is very interesting.<br /> <br /> They could work nicely in a Demon chronicle too I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T17:27:58-07:00","id":1492939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492935#post1492935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Akhem-Urtu were part of the Rite of Return. The Su-Menent screwed with their slice of it because they found out about the plan for the Shan'iatu Guildmasters to try and claim Judge Status over Life AND Death, but the explicit consequence of that is that the Shan'iatu were stuffed in with their servants.<br /> <br /> Endlessness is effectively the term for immortality not derived from the arts of Irem to those ends. Timelessness is explicitly the anti-relationship to time, and while it's usually a result of connection to Duat, disassociated from time as a rule, other forces can apply as well, such as the Deceived's relationship to Fate.<br /> <br /> And yeah, as BoLD goes, it's a hotfix. It updates everything that it updates, but doesn't assume everything else is left off the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the deceived don't goto duat, and don't go to the judges, they just stay in neter-kheret. I don't see how they also have timelessness, or how any of the others due.<br /> <br /> Unless we are arguing semantics. I thought timeless means explicitly that their immortality could take them anywhere in time. But it kinda sounds like you mean timelessness is related to memory, in which case I don't see how the maar-kherit are timeless","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T17:41:02-07:00","id":1492940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492939#post1492939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the deceived don't goto duat, and don't go to the judges, they just stay in neter-kheret. I don't see how they also have timelessness, or how any of the others due.<br /> <br /> Unless we are arguing semantics. I thought timeless means explicitly that their immortality could take them anywhere in time. But it kinda sounds like you mean timelessness is related to memory, in which case I don't see how the maar-kherit are timeless</div> </div> </div> </div>On the Deceived, see &quot;other forces can apply as well, such as the Deceived's relationship to Fate.&quot;<br /> <br /> On Timelessness, see &quot;explictly the anti-relationship to time&quot; and know I would say Memory if I meant Memory.<br /> <br /> Look, beyond explaining it to the best of my ability, all I can tell you that I run on the assumption that baselines established by the Arisen apply to the Minor Guilds unless otherwise stated. As is, the Kher-Minu and Wadjet-Itja are called out as explicitly not being Timeless, the Ahkem-Urtu and Maar-Kherit are not, so I take that as meaning they are Timeless. Everything else is me applying reasonable extrapolation and connection to the lore as it stands, particularly given the role the Deceived hold in Mummy's canon and pantheon of antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-12-2022, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T19:59:41-07:00","id":1492946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492940#post1492940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Deceived, see &amp;quot;other forces can apply as well, such as the Deceived's relationship to Fate.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> On Timelessness, see &amp;quot;explictly the anti-relationship to time&amp;quot; and know I would say Memory if I meant Memory.<br /> <br /> Look, beyond explaining it to the best of my ability, all I can tell you that I run on the assumption that baselines established by the Arisen apply to the Minor Guilds unless otherwise stated. As is, the Kher-Minu and Wadjet-Itja are called out as explicitly not being Timeless, the Ahkem-Urtu and Maar-Kherit are not, so I take that as meaning they are Timeless. Everything else is me applying reasonable extrapolation and connection to the lore as it stands, particularly given the role the Deceived hold in Mummy's canon and pantheon of antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha, but I didn't mean to offend you with the Memory thing. I was just making sure I wasn't misunderstanding. I will concede to the ahkem-urtu though, as it furthers how close they were with the rest of the major guilds in the Rite of return","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T20:03:03-07:00","id":1492947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1492939#post1492939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the deceived don't goto duat, and don't go to the judges, they just stay in neter-kheret.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> They're <i>barred from the one place in which a Deathless soul can be destroyed.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I thought timeless means explicitly that their immortality could take them anywhere in time. </div> </div> </div>The lexicon is pretty plainly phrased as a set of &quot;or&quot;s about an explicitly broad term, the easiest place to hide in Neter-Khertet (from, say, a gibbering ghostly stalker) is the swirling storm of sand and ash in its depths that utterly kills visibility, Memory doesn't work differently for the part of the Deceived that is a character, and carrying out their repose in Twilight does not make the process of resurrection go any faster.<br /> <br /> All the narrative tools exist for one of the Deceived to return to life before their last arrival if you are so inclined to use them for that purpose, and their starting kit doesn't bar them from the exact same tools the five major guilds have to perpetuate their Deathless immortality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T21:45:17-07:00","id":1492952,"title":"","content":"So rereading the Maar-Kherit how do they regain Sekhem? Not during when there awake but I mean when they wake and start there descent?<br /> <br /> With the deceived I assume it's the same and with the wadjet the judges as well as the Kher-Minu it's when there stuck as a statue the slowly regain Sekhem over time.<br /> <br /> I am assuming they get there sekhem via the Su-Menent ritual re energizing them when there sekhem hits zero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T23:40:48-07:00","id":1492958,"title":"","content":"The Maar-Kherit still serve the Judges, so it's that way.<br /> <br /> ALso that entire rejuvenating cancer probably has long term benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-13-2022, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T04:10:46-07:00","id":1492968,"title":"","content":"I like to think the Maar-Kherit exist as they are to ensure life continues to persist- the unfortunate circumstances of their genesis was a true blunder, but true Judges have found a use for them where the usurpers saw only a potential liability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 09-13-2022, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T04:02:53-07:00","id":1493813,"title":"","content":"If I may ask a couple more clarifications between editions, please. Some have been sorta answered, but for clarity's sake..<br /> <br /> 1. Can Decieved still not create Sadikh? In 1e, they couldnt, and instead had a slightly better cult. In 2e, all mummies get that improved Cult. Do Decieved get Sadikh now, or do they get an as of yet unrevealed Cult buff?<br /> <br /> 2. Do the Decieved still start with Ren 5 and all other pillars at 1, or are they as flexible as Arisen now?<br /> <br /> 3. How do you reflect the disease of the Maar-Kherit, in game? When someone gets Sybaris, they get the Sick tilt? The rest is normal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","user":"Cleverest of Things","date":". 09-27-2022, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T09:58:28-07:00","id":1493835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1493813#post1493813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may ask a couple more clarifications between editions, please. Some have been sorta answered, but for clarity's sake..<br /> <br /> 1. Can Decieved still not create Sadikh? In 1e, they couldnt, and instead had a slightly better cult. In 2e, all mummies get that improved Cult. Do Decieved get Sadikh now, or do they get an as of yet unrevealed Cult buff?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no mention of any of the minor guilds not having access to the Rite of the Engraved Heart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Do the Decieved still start with Ren 5 and all other pillars at 1, or are they as flexible as Arisen now? </div> </div> </div>Their defining Pillar is always Ren, but there is otherwise no special rule for their Pillar allocation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. How do you reflect the disease of the Maar-Kherit, in game? When someone gets Sybaris, they get the Sick tilt? The rest is normal? </div> </div> </div>No mechanics provided besides their Sybaris always starting at Stage 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T18:13:18-07:00","id":1494006,"title":"","content":"Another question, sorry for so many but Ive been waiting to ressurect my Decieved players, and started before I had all things straight.<br /> <br /> Decieved and Memory loss. Not the ones that happen during the Descent, but rather, during the escape. Because Decieved dont get the Drink of Lethe from Anpu, how does their Memory hold up from one Descent to the next? Does it still get degraded? Do they have a slight leg up over Arisen, on the front of Memory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T21:27:53-07:00","id":1494018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1494006#post1494006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question, sorry for so many but Ive been waiting to ressurect my Decieved players, and started before I had all things straight.<br /> <br /> Decieved and Memory loss. Not the ones that happen during the Descent, but rather, during the escape. Because Decieved dont get the Drink of Lethe from Anpu, how does their Memory hold up from one Descent to the next? Does it still get degraded? Do they have a slight leg up over Arisen, on the front of Memory?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Deceived do not have any special mechanics for Memory and the lack of the drink is counterbalanced by the lack of the Trials of Duat to give them freebies. The temakh's two most notable mechanical additions are giving the Deceived a second chance on roughly half their Descent rolls and periodically triggering a Clash to take over the sahu for a scene to do its own thing, including specifically sabotaging the character's personal projects.<br /> <br /> (The drink in Duat is also optional to provide a trade of extra starting Sekhem for an Absence, with refusal leaving the character with fragmentary memories of the Trials, so the Deceived don't really have much of a leg up from not getting that offer.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T13:01:55-07:00","id":1494546,"title":"","content":"While I do love to talk about the Deceived (and would point out that neither 1e or 2e interpretations give an opportunity for being Timeless<sup>1</sup>, since they exist as a conscious being within the main reality of Chronicles of Darkness; ie Earth and it's Twilight) and do not disagree with the idea that officially written words to the contrary all of the Minor Guild Arisen should have access to same stuff the corebook/&quot;Major&quot; Guilds do...it has started to dominate the thread a bit.<br /> <br /> We haven't even gotten to the part where we have playable Spirit characters yet. Or how broken the Purified are now. I thought those things were worth talking about.<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>As the Deceived are technically stuck within the 'normal' confines of the world, the &quot;lore&quot; suggests they can't qualify as Timeless as they wouldn't get an opportunity to jump to/from different points of time. However, as pointed out, there is no mention of this implied fact in the BoLD write up, let alone a mechanical line that spells it out. I would argue that the Deceived are still Eternal though; after all their existence is a contingency plan of demigods when the most powerful piece of time breaking sorcery went belly up. They exist now, forever and always.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T19:15:47-07:00","id":1494766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1494546#post1494546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I do love to talk about the Deceived (and would point out that neither 1e or 2e interpretations give an opportunity for being Timeless<sup>1</sup>, since they exist as a conscious being within the main reality of Chronicles of Darkness; ie Earth and it's Twilight) and do not disagree with the idea that officially written words to the contrary all of the Minor Guild Arisen should have access to same stuff the corebook/&quot;Major&quot; Guilds do...it has started to dominate the thread a bit.<br /> <br /> We haven't even gotten to the part where we have playable Spirit characters yet. Or how broken the Purified are now. I thought those things were worth talking about.<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>As the Deceived are technically stuck within the 'normal' confines of the world, the &quot;lore&quot; suggests they can't qualify as Timeless as they wouldn't get an opportunity to jump to/from different points of time. However, as pointed out, there is no mention of this implied fact in the BoLD write up, let alone a mechanical line that spells it out. I would argue that the Deceived are still Eternal though; after all their existence is a contingency plan of demigods when the most powerful piece of time breaking sorcery went belly up. They exist now, forever and always.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>I might get back to talking about things now that the badgering seems to have let up.<br /> <br /> But I will take this last thing on the subject of the Deceived to question the wisdom of not applying Timelessness to the splat that was literally the first to have it as a feature, ala the Fatewalker/Apotheosis Deceived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T12:56:18-07:00","id":1494803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1494766#post1494766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might get back to talking about things now that the badgering seems to have let up.<br /> <br /> But I will take this last thing on the subject of the Deceived to question the wisdom of not applying Timelessness to the splat that was literally the first to have it as a feature, ala the Fatewalker/Apotheosis Deceived.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many apologies for the &quot;badgering&quot;. I do wish the book had more wordcount, because there isn't anything that could be cut for space, its all interesting. That leaves some questions though. And we appreciate you taking the time to help us clarify some things. Still, we are only badgering you because there are definitely things unanswered by the book, and even this thread hasn't cleared up. I know a fuller answer is probably being saved for an antagonist book, and I can sympathize with your feeling badgered by the questions, especially if the answers ARE being kept quiet for a further book, or there are no answers. Ironically, I stopped the &quot;badgering&quot; because the answers were only &quot;mostly&quot; helpful, and a bit confusing, which is what led to further questions for clarification, ad naseum etc. Still, I dont want to annoy one of my favorite writers, so ill accept the answers arent coming until a later book and stop badgering. <br /> <br /> To add to the discussion and other aspects of the book, I absolutely LOVE how the Spirit World was portrayed. The Red Shore's neverending timeless everywhen moment of creation vibew fit really well with the timeless feel of the game. It, along with Colors from Void, can easily be used to cover some of the old 1e &quot;summoning eldritch/cthonic powers.&quot; I love that. My Decieved PC had gotten particularly attached to the Black Huriyah of 1e, so Im going to translate them as either Void-spirits or have a Black Huriyah painting/sculpture in his tomb to use to summon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T18:54:33-07:00","id":1494828,"title":"","content":"Okay, let's pick up on the takes:<br /> <br /> Out of the four Minor Guilds, the Maar-Kherit(aville) are probably the least personally exciting. They're a solid enough example of skeletons in the closet, decently tragic and driven, and the concept has enough breadth on it you could get a variety of characters out of it. Their tools are good and simple, one taking the Arisen toughness and ramping it up to 11, and the other one being a nifty risk/reward gamble for healing and plaguing. I suppose it's got the feeling of having been done before (even though it IS new to the Arisen's neck of the woods, and the flavor of the Physics is distinct from similar entitites). They're not bad, just not exciting.<br /> <br /> The Wadjet-Itja are about on par with the Kher-Minu in terms of my excitement for them. The juxtaposition of Oracles with Gamblers is the sort of thing that is all kinds of my jam*, but something about the bargaining for years is tired for me, and that almost took my interest in them out....only to get raised again by how the Thieves of Eyes are something your character is supposed to have an <i>opinion</i> on, ranging anywhere from &quot;Not really different from the Lifeless&quot; to &quot;Honorary Sixth Major Guild becuase the other major oracle guild was Deceived and these guys are stepping up.&quot; It's something that can likewise say soemthing about <i>your</i> character, even if the Wadjet-Itja never come up in game, which is a good piece to have. It helps that the Wadjet Itja are really versatile for moving up and down that range, making for good antagonists and allies in kind, all while still basically working from the same principles. Their guild Affiniities are effective and efficient, one being apretty direct fortune telling one, the other either facilitating or preventing cheating at any given gamble, and both providing tools to suck the life out of all the children of Salem. So, while they're not my ZOMG FAVORITE like I hoped, they're definitely fun.<br /> <br /> They give an example of character creation, and that's Chap 1. Nex up, Chap 2 starting with Judges judging you.<br /> <br /> *stop it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T13:34:49-07:00","id":1494885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1490415-the-book-of-everlasting-death-is-out?p=1494828#post1494828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, let's pick up on the takes:<br /> <br /> Out of the four Minor Guilds, the Maar-Kherit(aville) are probably the least personally exciting. They're a solid enough example of skeletons in the closet, decently tragic and driven, and the concept has enough breadth on it you could get a variety of characters out of it. Their tools are good and simple, one taking the Arisen toughness and ramping it up to 11, and the other one being a nifty risk/reward gamble for healing and plaguing. I suppose it's got the feeling of having been done before (even though it IS new to the Arisen's neck of the woods, and the flavor of the Physics is distinct from similar entitites). They're not bad, just not exciting.<br /> <br /> The Wadjet-Itja are about on par with the Kher-Minu in terms of my excitement for them. The juxtaposition of Oracles with Gamblers is the sort of thing that is all kinds of my jam*, but something about the bargaining for years is tired for me, and that almost took my interest in them out....only to get raised again by how the Thieves of Eyes are something your character is supposed to have an <i>opinion</i> on, ranging anywhere from &amp;quot;Not really different from the Lifeless&amp;quot; to &amp;quot;Honorary Sixth Major Guild becuase the other major oracle guild was Deceived and these guys are stepping up.&amp;quot; It's something that can likewise say soemthing about <i>your</i> character, even if the Wadjet-Itja never come up in game, which is a good piece to have. It helps that the Wadjet Itja are really versatile for moving up and down that range, making for good antagonists and allies in kind, all while still basically working from the same principles. Their guild Affiniities are effective and efficient, one being apretty direct fortune telling one, the other either facilitating or preventing cheating at any given gamble, and both providing tools to suck the life out of all the children of Salem. So, while they're not my ZOMG FAVORITE like I hoped, they're definitely fun.<br /> <br /> They give an example of character creation, and that's Chap 1. Nex up, Chap 2 starting with Judges judging you.<br /> <br /> *stop it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Maar-kherit could use some more dimensionality beyond &quot;oh God, please make it stop&quot;. But I actually only really liked them once I statted one up as an NPC for theoretical use later (I SWEAR DC comics has some kind of &quot;living plague/disease&quot; but I cant think of their name). To enhance the vibe of being an ancient doctor, I went all out on the healing and buffing. I found it interesting that the creature is leaking out massive amounts of life AND death. It can cure diseases, boost the body, raise the dead.. being near it is healing to those around it that can survive the sickness. And as mad as the agony has driven them, they are still a healer at heart, and might grant miracles to those who can get past its curse and touch its heart.<br /> <br /> I love the Kher-Minu. I immediatley knew one had to be guarding the artifact cache and smuggling operation in Gotham City Museum. Dangerous statue that comes to life in a musem, whats not to love? Of course, mechanically, I realized he couldnt be flying solo (with thst 100 year cooldown being rather nasty), so I paired him with a regular arisen &quot;handler&quot; that intercepts most smaller thefts and issues before it accidentally wakes the Knight in Shining Armor that protects the museum. I really like the way that the new Guilds' affinities work. To keep their injuries from eating away their Sekhem, you gotta find a way to survive, avoid damage, get it healed before it triggers the Sekhem.. a really quirky mechanic. <br /> <br /> Likewise, the quirk about the Wadjet-Itja. Im having a scary image of a Horoscope Hippie, obsessing over people's signs and doing readings and charts for their friends.. only to drop ACTUAL falling stars on people to steal their years. My other immediate image for a cool inspiration is Setzer from Final Fantasy 6. Bonus points for artifact throwing dice that do damage based on the actual physical dice roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-13T23:20:09-07:00","id":1494959,"title":"","content":"Been playing around with the Maar-Kherit, started up a character and so far I love how fast they can heal, especially with the fact that there healing affinity stacks already with seal the flesh and a mummies natural healing affinity.<br /> <br /> Beyond that after doing a session with the Maar-Kherit with the help of some affinities and utterances its become pretty apparent that they can regain pillars easily if you play them right. Seeing as this was a crossover game my PC came with a plot hook being that their virus was in remission it wasn't that infectious but it was still somewhat painful for them.<br /> <br /> On hand they were glad it was slowing down, on the other hand they realized that this may or may not be a one off thing and is currently spending there time in a long while conversing with non arisen and hoping to make some friends before the virus goes back into full swing.<br /> <br /> As for the Wadjet-Itja I do look them as gambling characters are a favorite for me especially the oracle aspect, but like ArcaneArt the stealing years and to extent lack of being achronal is a bit of a downside for me, perhaps trying to build a character should make it easier for me to enjoy them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T23:14:21-07:00","id":1495153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Liked the book,they really did all they could with the wordcount. Saw there was an updated final version. Though haven't noticed any major text differences. The section on the Shadow was absolutely fantastic, maybe the best part of the book overall.</div> </div> </div> </div>They added a new art near the intro and changed usurping the red shores tier 3, instead of all spirits going hostile right off the bat the arisen can spend a point of willpower to make them hostile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-15T08:51:58-08:00","id":1497177,"title":"","content":"Got it. Read it. Loved it.<br /> <br /> A comment, though...the Courtiers of Flesh are basically Cenobites, aren\u2019t they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base6